{
 "_doc": [
  "Raw composer inputs for web/connections.py compose(cfg, store, mail_runner_view, job_view, model_snapshot, vault_has, lockfile_busy, now). Lane A table-drives from this file; lane T1-A asserts the (state, code) in 'expect' for the item or row with that id.",
  "Each case lists ONLY the inputs it overrides: effective inputs = {**defaults, **case.inputs} (shallow per top-level key). Three shorthands expand into defaults.cfg: cfg_apply_mail -> cfg.apply_mail, cfg_apply_mail_backup -> cfg.apply_mail_backup, cfg_model {enable_llm, backend} -> cfg.budget_enable_llm / cfg.budget_backend.",
  "mail_accounts: full rows as store.mail_accounts() returns them (every column of CREATE TABLE mail_accounts). ats_accounts: full rows as store.accounts() returns them (every column of CREATE TABLE ats_accounts, vault_service included; the composer must never send it).",
  "mail_runner: the view of request.app.state.mail: {timer_running, status:{running, started_at, next_at}} (web/mailsync.py). job_view (ASSUMED shape; adjust together with lane A): {current: jobs.current(tail=0) reduced to {state, kind} or null; attempts_in_flight: store.attempts_in_flight(); last_attempts: store.last_attempts()}. model_snapshot: ModelHealth.snapshot() as {ok, code, backend, model, local, checked_at}, or null before the first probe (-> checking/probing).",
  "vault_has: booleans only, keyed '<vault service>|<username>' (service = vault.imap_service(host) for mailboxes, the row's vault_service for employer accounts). A missing key means False. No password or secret appears anywhere in these fixtures.",
  "edge: {profile_dir_exists, lockfile_busy} stand in for the is_dir() check and the lockfile read test. now: the clock the 24 h rules use.",
  "expect.id: the item id (gmail:<mail_accounts.id>, gmail for none, apply-mailbox, apply-mailbox:backup, employer-accounts, edge, model) or 'account:<ats_accounts.id>' for a row of employer_accounts[] (its per-row state/code). Assert only the item/row with that id; other items in the composed response are not specified by the case.",
  "need_now_* cases pin the exact rule of section 2.3 (a to d plus two negatives); the snapshot there is 'unreachable', so need_now flips neutral to attention."
 ],
